--- body ---
## Context
The spec marks `Tags` as repeatable — one `Tags:` line per value, like `Blocked-by:`.
The plural name `Tags:` implies a non-repeatable list on a single line (e.g. CSV),
which is the opposite of how it works. The existing convention in this format is
singular names for repeatable headers (`Blocked-by:`, not `Blocked-bys:`).
Rename to `Tag:` for consistency; repeatability is kept.

## Actions
1. Spec: rename `Tags` row in the headers table and update prose in `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`.
2. Definition layer: rename `Tags` → `Tag` in `ValidHeaders` and update the ABNF comments and `ValidTagValues` doc in `src/go/ergspecv1.go`.
3. Parser/accessor: rename `Erg.Tags()` → `Erg.Tag()`, switch the underlying header key, update call site in `src/go/ready.go`. The JSON struct field `Tags []string` (the array name in the wire format) is preserved.
4. Validator: emit a migration hint when an old `Tags:` header is encountered (analogous to the `Status:` hint), and update rule 3a + rule 5 doc comments to say `Tag:`.
5. Migration: extend `erg migrate` to rewrite preamble `Tags:` lines to `Tag:` (preamble-bounded, idempotent), with a separate counter and matching summary text.
6. Embedded assets: regenerate the base64 blobs in `src/go/bootstrap_assets.go` after spec and AGENTS.md changes.
7. Tests: update the existing `Tags value not in closed set` case; add a new case asserting the migration hint; update shell-test fixtures and grep patterns in `tests/test_validate.sh`, `tests/test_ready.sh`, `tests/test_check.sh`; add a `Tags:` → `Tag:` migration round-trip case in `tests/test_migrate.sh`.
8. Regenerate `docs/erg-manual.md` via `make docs`.
9. Migrate existing tickets with `build/erg migrate tickets/`. No preamble `Tags:` lines exist in the corpus (only code-block illustrations inside the body of `tickets/closed/0015-tags-header.erg`), so the migration is a no-op against real headers; the command exits 0.

## Test
```bash
grep -rn '^Tags:' tickets/   # only literal preamble Tags: lines; expect 0 outside body code blocks
build/erg validate <(printf '%%erg v1\nTitle: X\nCreated: 2024-01-01\nAuthor: t\nTags: needs-human\n\n--- log ---\n--- body ---\n') 2>&1 | grep "renamed to 'Tag:'"
```
Validator: a file with `Tags: needs-human` is rejected with a clear error pointing to `erg migrate`.
Migrator: a preamble `Tags:` line is rewritten to `Tag:` while body code blocks containing `Tags:` are preserved.

## Exit criteria
- `Tag:` is the header name in spec, code, and all ticket preambles.
- `erg migrate` rewrites preamble `Tags:` → `Tag:` cleanly and is idempotent.
- Validator emits a clear migration hint when it encounters a `Tags:` preamble line.
- `make test` passes.
- PR body documents the migration approach and audit count.
